label ch30_49:
    [   0] m "Gosh, I used to be so ignorant about certain things..."
    [   1] m "When I was in middle school, I thought that taking medication was an easy way out, or something like that."
    [   2] m "Like anyone could just solve their mental problems with enough willpower..."
    [   3] m "I guess if you don't suffer from a mental illness, it's not possible to know what it's really like."
    [   4] m "Are there some disorders that are over-diagnosed? Probably...I never really looked into it, though."
    [   5] m "But that doesn't change the fact that a lot of them go undiagnosed too, you know?"
    [   6] m "But medication aside...people even look down on seeing a mental health professional."
    [   7] m "Like, sorry that I want to learn more about my own mind, right?"
    [   8] m "Everyone has all kinds of struggles and stresses...and professionals dedicate their lives to helping with those."
    [   9] m "If you think it could help you become a better person, don't be shy to consider something like that."
    [  10] m "We're on a never-ending journey to improve ourselves, you know?"
    [  11] m "Well...I say that, but I think you're pretty perfect already."
